SUMMARY:Book Babies
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Fridays at 9:45 a.m. for special bonding time 
 with your little one (ages 0-24 months)! At this lapsit-style storytime\, 
 we will spend about 20 minutes engaging in structured learning through 
 bounces\, rhymes\, songs\, and books\, followed by 15-45 minutes of 
 unstructured play and socialization time.\n\nNote: A television is used 
 during the first part of the program to display the words to the songs and 
 rhymes (to support adult engagement)\; there are no moving pictures. \n\nTo 
 celebrate 2026 Summer Reading and its theme\, "Unearth a Story\," we will 
 be focusing on dinosaurs from June 12 - August 7\, 2026.\n\nAll are 
 welcome! If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact Chelsea at cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible!\n
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16508934
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16508934
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260626T140000Z
DTEND:20260626T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260626T000000Z
SUMMARY:Restorative Yoga
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a class for adults that will provide an opportunity 
 for you to relax through gentle stretching and mindful breathing. This 
 class is designed for anyone who would like to slow down\, connect with the 
 body and calm the mind. Both beginners and experienced yogis are welcome. 
 During the class\, you will be guided through a series of yoga poses and 
 mindful breathing techniques intended to calm the busy mind and stretch the 
 body. Registration is required. \n\nPlease provide your own mat or a 
 towel.\n\nIf you have questions about accessibility\, program stimulation 
 levels\, and/or need disability accommodations\, please contact us at 
 919-560-7192.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carmen Ruth":MAILTO:cruth@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness, Sensory Friendly
UID:LibCal-14288-16640123
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16640123
END:VEVENT
