SUMMARY:Read to Me Pet Partners
DESCRIPTION:Relax and read with a dog and other animals! This program 
 brings dogs and other animals together with emergent readers for 15 minutes 
 of companionship. Handlers and their dogs provide quiet encouragement to 
 children so that they might develop a love of reading and improve 
 communication skills. \n\nThis program is geared towards elementary 
 students\, but all ages are welcome! This program will be held on 
 Saturday\, June 27\, 2026\, from 10a.m.- 12p.m at North Regional Library. 
 The address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.\n\nPlease note that you 
 may book one session per day\, and sessions are 15 minutes long. Available 
 time slots are as follows: 10: 00a.m\, 10: 20a.m\, and 10:30a.m. 
 \n\nRegistration is required. Please call Molly at 919-560-0234 or email 
 mschaefer@dconc.gov with your preferred day/ time and your contact 
 information.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
