SUMMARY:Bilingual Storytime at The Nasher / Cuento Bilingüe en el Museo de Arte Nasher
DESCRIPTION:First Thursday of each month at 10:30 & 11:00 AM\n\nFREE! ~ 
 GRATIS!\n\nJoin Durham County Library for our monthly Bilingual Story Time 
 at the Nasher Museum of Art. Settle into our galleries for a fun story read 
 in Spanish and English\, followed by a short discussion about an artwork 
 and related art making activity. This program is free for kids ages 1 – 5 
 and their adult caregivers.\n\n*Registration Required only for groups of 8 
 or more must be in advance by emailing 
 nashered@duke.edu\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEl 
 primer jueves de cada mes a las 10:30 y 11:00 a. m.\n\nGRATIS! ~ 
 FREE!\n\nÚnase a la Biblioteca del Condado de Durham para nuestro Cuento 
 Bilingüe mensual en el Museo de Arte Nasher. Acomódate en en las 
 galerías para escuchar un cuento divertido en Español e Inglés\, seguida 
 por una breve conversación y actividad de arte.\n\nEste programa es 
 gratuito para niños de 1 a 5 años y sus cuidadores adultos.\n\n*Se 
 requiere inscripción solo para grupos de 8 o más personas\, debe 
 realizarse con anticipación enviando un correo electrónico a 
 nashered@duke.edu
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Patty Melendez":MAILTO:pmelendez@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Bilingual, Spanish, Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-15318478
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15318478
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260702T143000Z
DTEND:20260702T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260702T000000Z
SUMMARY:Liv and Sing!
DESCRIPTION:Ms. Olivia invites you to lively\, assorted music\, sit-down 
 moments\, energetic dancing and closing scarf-movement. All ages welcome.\n
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Olivia Singleton":MAILTO:osingleton@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Music
UID:LibCal-14288-15559126
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15559126
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260702T143000Z
DTEND:20260702T151500Z
DTSTAMP:20260702T000000Z
SUMMARY:Storytime with Ms. Chloe
DESCRIPTION:Come join us in the Children's Programming Room for Storytime 
 with Ms. Chloe. This is a noisy Storytime that will be full of reading\, 
 singing\, dancing\, rhythm sticks\, and bubbles! \n\nAfterwards we will 
 play with dinosaurs and coloring pages.\n\nGeared towards toddlers to 
 Kindergarteners\, but all ages are welcome to join in the fun!\n\nChildren 
 under the age of 10 must be supervised by an adult.\n\nFor more 
 information\, contact: chloebullock@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-15624785
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15624785
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260702T143000Z
DTEND:20260702T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260702T000000Z
SUMMARY:Page Turners Club
DESCRIPTION:Page Turners Club is a fun and engaging summer reading program 
 for rising 2nd and 3rd graders. Join us every Tuesday and Thursday this 
 summer as we explore exciting stories\, build reading confidence\, and 
 discover the joy of books through read-alouds\, activities\, games\, and 
 prizes. Whether your child already loves reading or is just beginning their 
 reading journey\, Page Turners Club is a welcoming space to grow 
 imagination\, friendship\, and a lifelong love of reading.\n\nSnacks will 
 be provided!\n\nRegistration is required! \n
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Side 2\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalia Lucena-Trujillo":MAILTO:nltrujillo@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16796369
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16796369
END:VEVENT
