SUMMARY:Playdough Playtime (Ages 2-6)
DESCRIPTION:Join us to build and play with our collection of colorful 
 Play-Doh and sculpting toys! This is a fun\, sensory playtime to foster 
 creativity and exploration while building fine motor skills. This program 
 is geared towards children ages 2-6 and their caregivers. \n\nDoes your 
 little one have an allergy to gluten? We can provide kinetic sand and 
 sanitized tools. Please reach out to Kristen at kstockdale@dconc.gov prior 
 to this program for accommodations. \n\nAll supplies provided. Registration 
 is appreciated but not required. \n
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Arts & Crafts, High & Low Sensory Stimulation, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-15991623
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15991623
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260702T151500Z
DTEND:20260702T161500Z
DTSTAMP:20260702T000000Z
SUMMARY:Your Family Tree: Help from an Experienced Local Genealogist
DESCRIPTION:Do you want to learn more about your family tree? Whether 
 you're just getting started or have been researching your family for 
 years\, you can benefit from a one-hour personalized session with an expert 
 genealogist. These sessions will be held on Thursday mornings at 10 and 11 
 a.m.\, June 18 & 25 and July 2 & 9. Sign up now!
LOCATION:North Study Room #1\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Emily Tobias":MAILTO:etobias@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Digital/Tech Literacy, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16810405
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16810405
END:VEVENT
