DTSTAMP:20260708T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: A Marriage at Sea
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 A Marriage at Sea by Sophie Elmhirst. The description for the book is 
 below:\n"The electrifying true story of a young couple shipwrecked at sea: 
 a mind-blowing tale of obsession\, survival\, and partnership stretched to 
 its limits. Maurice and Maralyn make an odd couple. He's a loner\, awkward 
 and obsessive\; she's charismatic and ambitious. But they share a horror of 
 wasting their lives. And they dream--as we all dream--of running away from 
 it all. What if they quit their jobs\, sold their house\, bought a boat\, 
 and sailed away?\n\nMost of us begin and end with the daydream. But Maurice 
 began to study nautical navigation. Maralyn made detailed lists of 
 provisions. And in June 1972\, they set sail. For nearly a year all went 
 well\, until deep in the Pacific\, a breaching whale knocked a hole in 
 their boat and it sank beneath the waves. What ensues is a jaw-dropping 
 fight to survive on the wild ocean\, with little hope of rescue. Alone 
 together for months in a tiny rubber raft\, starving and exhausted\, 
 Maurice and Maralyn have to find not only ways to stay alive but ways to 
 get along\, as their inner demons emerge and their marriage is put to the 
 greatest of tests. Although they could run away from the world\, they can't 
 run away from themselves.\n\nTaut\, propulsive\, and dazzling\, A Marriage 
 At Sea pairs adrenaline-fueled high seas adventure with a gutting love 
 story that asks why we love difficult people\, and who we become under the 
 most extreme conditions imaginable."\n\nWe look forward to seeing you all 
 soon!\n\n\nInterested in attending a future Daytime Book Club meeting? Take 
 a look at our reading list below:\n\nMay 2026: To the Lighthouse by 
 Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: The Night Watchman by Louise Erdrich\n\nJuly 
 2026: A Marriage at Sea by Sophie Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: My Friends by 
 Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 2026: Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte 
 McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on Mango Street by Sandra 
 Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil by John 
 Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What 
 We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: Song of Solomon by Toni 
 Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by 
 Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576125
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576125
END:VEVENT
