SUMMARY:Homeschool Learning Lab: Calm-a-saurus Zen Garden
DESCRIPTION:Take a moment to slow down! Zen gardens are designed to 
 encourage relaxation and quiet reflection. With the fast pace of summer\, 
 it can feel like an art just to calm the mind. Stop by and create your own 
 calming\, dinosaur-themed mini garden to take home or display on your desk. 
 Best for children ages 5 and up but all are welcome. \n\nThis program will 
 be held at North Regional Library Thursday\, July 9\, 2026\, at 10a.m. The 
 address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.   \n\nThis event will be held 
 outside\, weather permitting\, so please dress accordingly. \n\nHomeschool 
 Learning Lab meets weekly year-round. In the summer\, we ask for 
 registration in order to help with program prep. Please register each child 
 attending. \n\nIf you have any questions\, accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact Molly at mschaefer@dconc.gov.  We ask 
 that all requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to the 
 event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Homeschool, Summer Reading
