BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
DTSTAMP:20260710T000000Z
SUMMARY:Donut Stop Me Now: Donut Crawl
DESCRIPTION:Get out in your local community and eat some great donuts (and 
 other treats) this summer!\n\nPick up your Donut Tracker from any Durham 
 County Library location or emails Sara Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to 
 receive a PDF of the tracker. The Donut Crawl runs from June 5th (National 
 Donut Day!) through August 1st. You'll earn a completion sticker for each 
 donut location you visit. Completion stickers are available at Durham 
 County Library locations. Visit 5 or more locations to be entered into the 
 final prize drawing for a 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets! Please complete a 
 tracker for each member of your party who participates.\n\nTrackers must be 
 turned into a Durham County Library Location by Saturday\, August 8th to be 
 entered into the final prize drawing.\n\nRegistration not required. Open to 
 all ages.\n\n \n\nDonut Stop Me Now Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWhat is 
 the Donut Crawl?\n\nThe Donut Crawl is an opportunity for patrons to 
 explore Durham while supporting local businesses. During the course of the 
 8 weeks\, patrons are asked to visit as many donut locations as they can. 
 Those who visit 5 or more locations will be entered into a raffle to win a 
 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets.\n\nWho can participate in the Donut 
 Crawl?\n\nAnyone can participate in the Donut Crawl. It is open to all 
 ages. There is no registration required. A Durham County Library card is 
 not required.\n\nWhat do I need to get started?\n\nEach person 
 participating in the crawl will need a Donut Crawl tracker. Trackers may be 
 picked up at any Durham County Library location or you can email Sara 
 Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to receive a PDF of the tracker. \n\nDo I have 
 to purchase something from each place I visit?\n\nWe understand everyone 
 comes from a different financial background. Please purchase what you can 
 to support local businesses\, but please do not hurt your own budget. 
 \n\nWhat do I need to do after I visit a donut place?\n\nYou'll mark off 
 the location on your donut tracker. It's an honor system. The donut places 
 themselves do not check off your tracker. For each place you visit\, you'll 
 receive a sticker. Stickers can be picked up at any Durham County Library 
 location.\n\nHow do I enter the Grand Prize Raffle?\n\nYou must visit 5 or 
 more donut places and turn in your completed tracker to any Durham County 
 Library location.\n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Community Engagement, Food & Cooking
UID:LibCal-14288-16828894
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16828894
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260710T134500Z
DTEND:20260710T143000Z
DTSTAMP:20260710T000000Z
SUMMARY:Book Babies
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Fridays at 9:45 a.m. for special bonding time 
 with your little one (ages 0-24 months)! At this lapsit-style storytime\, 
 we will spend about 20 minutes engaging in structured learning through 
 bounces\, rhymes\, songs\, and books\, followed by 15-45 minutes of 
 unstructured play and socialization time.\n\nNote: A television is used 
 during the first part of the program to display the words to the songs and 
 rhymes (to support adult engagement)\; there are no moving pictures. \n\nTo 
 celebrate 2026 Summer Reading and its theme\, "Unearth a Story\," we will 
 be focusing on dinosaurs from June 12 - August 7\, 2026.\n\nAll are 
 welcome! If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact Chelsea at cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible!\n
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16508936
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16508936
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260710T140000Z
DTEND:20260710T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260710T000000Z
SUMMARY:Memory Cafe
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a monthly activity for people with dementia 
 and their caregivers. Memory Cafes host activities designed to engage in 
 the present\, without the expectations of using short-term memory or 
 forward thinking. This month\, we will celebrate summer reading by making 
 dinosaur imprints! Get ready to get messy as we use figurines\, texture 
 plates\, and molds to make a fossil keepsake out of clay! \n\nThis program 
 will be held on July 10\, 2026\, at 10 a.m. at the North Regional Library 
 in the Small Program Room. The address is 221 Milton Rd.\n\nIf you have any 
 accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact me at 
 dpeterson@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least three (3) 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible! Please email me if you plan to attend and have nut 
 allergies so that we can make accommodations.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Desiree Peterson":MAILTO:dpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Low Sensory Stimulation, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16885337
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16885337
END:VEVENT
