SUMMARY:Crafting for Littles: Sensory Play with Paint
DESCRIPTION:Babies and toddlers up to 2 years old (and their caregivers!) 
 are welcome to join us on the 2nd and 4th Friday of every month this summer 
 for some very simple crafts! Crafting encourages babies and toddlers to 
 exercise their fine motor skills and eye-hand coordination\, develop their 
 critical thinking skills\, and get creative!\n\nThis week\, we will make 
 paintings while enjoying some sensory play! We will use cling wrap or 
 sandwich bags to PAT\, SHAKE\, and SQUISH paint onto canvases or cardstock 
 paper\, mostly mess-free!\n\nRegistration is required.\n\nIf you have any 
 questions\, please contact us @ 919-560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Perez":MAILTO:natperez@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Summer Reading
