SUMMARY:Donut Stop Me Now: Donut Crawl
DESCRIPTION:Get out in your local community and eat some great donuts (and 
 other treats) this summer!\n\nPick up your Donut Tracker from any Durham 
 County Library location or emails Sara Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to 
 receive a PDF of the tracker. The Donut Crawl runs from June 5th (National 
 Donut Day!) through August 1st. You'll earn a completion sticker for each 
 donut location you visit. Completion stickers are available at Durham 
 County Library locations. Visit 5 or more locations to be entered into the 
 final prize drawing for a 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets! Please complete a 
 tracker for each member of your party who participates.\n\nTrackers must be 
 turned into a Durham County Library Location by Saturday\, August 8th to be 
 entered into the final prize drawing.\n\nRegistration not required. Open to 
 all ages.\n\n \n\nDonut Stop Me Now Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWhat is 
 the Donut Crawl?\n\nThe Donut Crawl is an opportunity for patrons to 
 explore Durham while supporting local businesses. During the course of the 
 8 weeks\, patrons are asked to visit as many donut locations as they can. 
 Those who visit 5 or more locations will be entered into a raffle to win a 
 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets.\n\nWho can participate in the Donut 
 Crawl?\n\nAnyone can participate in the Donut Crawl. It is open to all 
 ages. There is no registration required. A Durham County Library card is 
 not required.\n\nWhat do I need to get started?\n\nEach person 
 participating in the crawl will need a Donut Crawl tracker. Trackers may be 
 picked up at any Durham County Library location or you can email Sara 
 Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to receive a PDF of the tracker. \n\nDo I have 
 to purchase something from each place I visit?\n\nWe understand everyone 
 comes from a different financial background. Please purchase what you can 
 to support local businesses\, but please do not hurt your own budget. 
 \n\nWhat do I need to do after I visit a donut place?\n\nYou'll mark off 
 the location on your donut tracker. It's an honor system. The donut places 
 themselves do not check off your tracker. For each place you visit\, you'll 
 receive a sticker. Stickers can be picked up at any Durham County Library 
 location.\n\nHow do I enter the Grand Prize Raffle?\n\nYou must visit 5 or 
 more donut places and turn in your completed tracker to any Durham County 
 Library location.\n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Community Engagement, Food & Cooking
UID:LibCal-14288-16828895
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16828895
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260711T140000Z
DTEND:20260711T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260711T000000Z
SUMMARY:Arts for Autism Presents: Kids' Sensory Painting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a casual art drop-in with Arts for Autism! We will 
 explore painting through texture and touch. \n\nChildren of all ages are 
 welcome. (Caregivers must remain present with their children.)\n\nArts for 
 Autism is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization dedicated to creating 
 inclusive\, equitable\, and intentional arts based learning opportunities 
 to children and adolescents on the spectrum. They have hosted events all 
 across North Carolina\, and are excited to continue programming at a 
 library near you!\n\n\n\nIf you have questions about accessibility\, 
 program stimulation levels\, and/or need disability accommodations\, please 
 contact the Library at Accessibility_Services@dconc.gov or 919-560-0183.
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Accessibility Services":MAILTO:accessibility_services@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Arts & Crafts, Community Engagement, High & Low Sensory Stimulation
UID:LibCal-14288-16767996
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16767996
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260711T140000Z
DTEND:20260711T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260711T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mindful Yoga
DESCRIPTION:Inhale\, exhale\, and join us for a Mindful Yoga class at 
 Durham East Regional Library!\n\nThis class offers a slower\, reflective 
 approach to yoga that integrates gentle movement\, breathwork\, rest\, and 
 brief exploration of yogic philosophy. Expect an accessible\, non-strenuous 
 practice that emphasizes steadiness\, ease\, and mindfulness — both on 
 and off the mat.\n\nPlease bring a yoga mat to use at the program. Spare 
 yoga mats are available while supplies last. Space is limited. Registration 
 is required.\n\nIf you have questions about accessibility and/or need 
 accommodations\, please contact Mara (she/her): mplantholt@dconc.gov or 
 919-560-0207.\n\n\nAbout the presenter:\n\nRohini Rajgopal is a certified 
 yoga instructor trained through Kaivalyadhama\, one of India’s oldest 
 yoga institutes. Her teaching is rooted in classical yogic principles and 
 emphasizes yoga as a holistic practice — not just physical postures — 
 creating space for reflection\, breath\, and embodied awareness.
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-16938332
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16938332
END:VEVENT
