DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
SUMMARY:Donut Stop Me Now: Donut Crawl
DESCRIPTION:Get out in your local community and eat some great donuts (and 
 other treats) this summer!\n\nPick up your Donut Tracker from any Durham 
 County Library location or emails Sara Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to 
 receive a PDF of the tracker. The Donut Crawl runs from June 5th (National 
 Donut Day!) through August 1st. You'll earn a completion sticker for each 
 donut location you visit. Completion stickers are available at Durham 
 County Library locations. Visit 5 or more locations to be entered into the 
 final prize drawing for a 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets! Please complete a 
 tracker for each member of your party who participates.\n\nTrackers must be 
 turned into a Durham County Library Location by Saturday\, August 8th to be 
 entered into the final prize drawing.\n\nRegistration not required. Open to 
 all ages.\n\n \n\nDonut Stop Me Now Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWhat is 
 the Donut Crawl?\n\nThe Donut Crawl is an opportunity for patrons to 
 explore Durham while supporting local businesses. During the course of the 
 8 weeks\, patrons are asked to visit as many donut locations as they can. 
 Those who visit 5 or more locations will be entered into a raffle to win a 
 4-pack of Durham Bulls tickets.\n\nWho can participate in the Donut 
 Crawl?\n\nAnyone can participate in the Donut Crawl. It is open to all 
 ages. There is no registration required. A Durham County Library card is 
 not required.\n\nWhat do I need to get started?\n\nEach person 
 participating in the crawl will need a Donut Crawl tracker. Trackers may be 
 picked up at any Durham County Library location or you can email Sara 
 Gibson at sgibson@dconc.gov to receive a PDF of the tracker. \n\nDo I have 
 to purchase something from each place I visit?\n\nWe understand everyone 
 comes from a different financial background. Please purchase what you can 
 to support local businesses\, but please do not hurt your own budget. 
 \n\nWhat do I need to do after I visit a donut place?\n\nYou'll mark off 
 the location on your donut tracker. It's an honor system. The donut places 
 themselves do not check off your tracker. For each place you visit\, you'll 
 receive a sticker. Stickers can be picked up at any Durham County Library 
 location.\n\nHow do I enter the Grand Prize Raffle?\n\nYou must visit 5 or 
 more donut places and turn in your completed tracker to any Durham County 
 Library location.\n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Community Engagement, Food & Cooking
UID:LibCal-14288-16828896
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16828896
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260712T133000Z
DTEND:20260712T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
SUMMARY:Roaming Readers: A Walking Audiobook Club!
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we walk the trails of RTP while listening to 
 audiobooks! After\, feel free to join us at Drift Coffee Shop & Kitchen RTP 
 for an optional discussion about the book and a chance to meet new 
 people.\n\n \n\nThis month’s suggested audiobook is Where the Crawdads 
 Sing (available on Libby). If you have already read it\, or would prefer 
 another title\, we suggest: Telephone by Percival Everett (available on 
 Libby and Hoopla) or Long After We Are Gone by Terah Shelton Harris 
 (available on Libby and Hoopla). \n\n \n\nThis event is for book lovers\, 
 the book-curious\, people who haven’t been able to make time to read (or 
 listen) for fun\, introverts\, extroverts\, exercisers\, caregivers pushing 
 strollers\, (leashed) dog owners\, groups\, singles\, nature lovers\, and 
 multi-taskers!\n\n \n\nAll paces welcome\, please take breaks when you need 
 them. We know it is easy to get transported to another world when listening 
 to your book. Be sure to stay alert as we will be crossing roads and may 
 encounter uneven pavement. \n\n \n\nWhile attendance is free\, please 
 register here to receive reminders and stay in the know for any updates. 
 Free public parking is located on the deck just across the street at 3150 
 Elion Drive. We will meet at 3151 Elion Drive Durham\, NC 27713.\n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Email Elle at kfarmer@dconc.gov.\n\n \n\nUpcoming 
 dates:\n\nAugust 9th\n\nSeptember 13th
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16545992
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16545992
END:VEVENT
