SUMMARY:Ready\, Set\, Baby (Spanish) at Southwest Regional Library
DESCRIPTION:Clases prenatales gratuitas sobre lactancia materna\, 
 diseñadas para ayudar a las familias a prepararse para la llegada de un 
 nuevo bebé\, ya sean padres primerizos o que estén ampliando su familia. 
 Estas clases son una excelente manera de prepararse para el embarazo\, el 
 parto y la vida con un recién nacido. Recibirá información útil sobre 
 la lactancia materna\, el cuidado posparto y qué esperar durante las 
 primeras semanas. Nuestra clase está repleta de charlas\, recursos y ¡un 
 obsequio al final! Se ofrecerán refrigerios. Cupo limitado. ¡Inscríbase 
 en línea!\n\n \n\nReady\, Set\, Baby Classes:  Free prenatal breastfeeding 
 education class designed to help you get ready for your baby\, whether you 
 are a first-time parent or adding to your family. These classes are a great 
 way to prepare for pregnancy\, birth\, and life with a newborn. You’ll 
 get helpful information on breastfeeding\, postpartum care\, and what to 
 expect in those early weeks. Our class is packed with conversations\, 
 resources\, and a raffle prize at the end! You’ll have a chance to win 
 amazing prizes like:\n\n\n	Breast pumps\n	Diaper bags filled with baby 
 essentials\n	Car seats\n	Breastfeeding pillows\n	…and more! 
 \n\n\nRegistration required. Questions? Please contact Jasmine at 
 jjohnson@dconc.gov. \n\n \n\nCan't make it to this location? These classes 
 will be held at all Durham County locations over the next couple of months. 
 See our calendar for the upcoming dates at the other locations!
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-16779802
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16779802
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260714T223000Z
DTEND:20260714T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260714T000000Z
SUMMARY:POSTPONED - Food Fibs: Agriculture Misinformation with Cooperative Extension
DESCRIPTION:Due to scheduling changes\, this event with Coopertive 
 Extension is now POSTPONED to Tuesday\, September 1st from 6-7:30pm. Please 
 register for the September 1st date here - 
 https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17186355\n\nThank you!\n\nEver 
 feel confused about information and misinformation surroudning agriculture 
 and nutrition? Join us for a program and discussion about misinformation 
 and agriculture! This presentation will discuss common misconceptions and 
 myths associated with agriculture in North Carolina and the country as a 
 whole. Lead by agents from the North Carolina Cooperative Extension in 
 Durham\, this program will have a presenation for the first portion of the 
 program time\, followed by Q&A and more discussion. Feel free to bring 
 questions and participate in discussion together.\n\nRegistration is 
 required. The content of this program will be geared towards adults and 
 teens.\n\nThis event will take place in the Innovation Lab on third floor 
 of Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701).\n\nNote: If you 
 have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us 
 at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 3 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible!
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Durham, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16526541
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16526541
END:VEVENT
