SUMMARY:World-building 101 (Setting Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:Often neglected\, world-building can make a profound difference 
 in your stories. This workshop will discuss everything from development 
 theory to implementation strategies\, as well as how to avoid common 
 pitfalls when weaving the background of your future novel (helpful for any 
 genre\, essential for speculative fiction).   \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Phillip Locey":MAILTO:plocey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Writing
