SUMMARY:Cretaceous Carolina: Prehistoric Life in the Tar Heel State
DESCRIPTION:Learn what prehistoric life was like in North Carolina\, what 
 species lived here\, what fossils have been found in this area\, and more 
 in this presentation from North Carolina Fossil Club member Joy Herrington! 
 An avid collector herself\, Joy will be bringing a number of fossils from 
 her own collection for you to explore.\n\nPlease note that this program is 
 for older teens and adults. Browse our event calendar for tons of dinosaur 
 and fossil-related programs for children!\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Summer Reading
