BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260722T220000Z
DTEND:20260722T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260722T000000Z
SUMMARY:HELL PIGS: Prehistoric Beasts of North Carolina
DESCRIPTION:Join Durham County Library for a journey to the distant past 
 where great beasts strode the lands and North Carolina was the domain of 
 mighty creatures known as the HELL PIGS. \n\nMuch of North Carolina’s 
 fossil record over the last 100 million years is derived from marine 
 environments\, often excluding fossils from terrestrial ecosystems. New 
 fossils collected from Jones County and deposited in the early Miocene\, 
 about 20 million years ago\, are beginning to shed light on an unusual land 
 mammal fauna from our state that includes hell pigs\, red pandas\, 
 rhinos.\n\nHear Sean Moran\, Collection Manager for Paleontology & Geology 
 describe these magnificent creatures and the world they lived in and gain a 
 glimpse into a very different era of North Carolina history. \n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Environmental, STEAM, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16630910
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16630910
END:VEVENT

